The standard place to look for UseNet posting rules is the
group news.announce.newusers and go back through the archives
to 1999 when the standard set of postings was still regularly
posted.  The group is still active with a post today that
points to web pages with the old posts.  I suspect these
postings stopped because by 1999 the rules could no longer
be enforced (consider - if there were no police would murder
still be condemned?  no longer enforcible is not the same as
no longer in existance).

I just looked through them and I could not find any reference
to "OT" "[OT]" or "OT:".  That standard has emerged since 1999
and is on a per-group basis.  It is recognized by any UseNet
regular but it remains informal at this point, likely because
there is no longer a formal method of updating the global
useNet rules.


